Question 1: Allocation of Expenses and Incomes to Cost Centres
Practical Question:
Shree Enterprises has two departments: Sales Department and Administration
Department. Allocate an offi ce expense of ₹40,000 between the two cost centres in the
ratio of 60:40.
Answer Steps:
1. Go to F11 → Accounting → Enable Cost Centres.
2. Create a Sales Department and Administration Department as Cost Centres.
3. Create/verify the Offi ce Expenses ledger and enable cost centre allocation.
4. Go to Accounting Vouchers → Payment (F5).
5. Select Offi ce Expenses and enter ₹40,000.
6. In the Cost Centre Allocation screen, enter:
○ Sales Department – ₹24,000
○ Administration Department – ₹16,000
7. Save the voucher.
8. View Cost Centre Reports to verify the allocation.
Question 2: Automation of Cost Centre Allocation Using Cost Centre
Classes
Practical Question:
Shree Enterprises wants to automatically allocate Telephone Expenses between the Sales and Administration departments in the ratio of 70:30. Create a Cost Centre Class and
record the expense using automatic allocation.
Answer Steps:
1. Go to F11 → Accounting → Enable Cost Centres.
2. Create Sales Department and Administration Department cost centres.
3. Go to Cost Centre Class → Create.
4. Name the class Telephone Expense Allocation.
5. Set the allocation:
○ Sales Department – 70%
○ Administration Department – 30%
6. Create/alter the Telephone Expenses ledger and enable Cost Centre Allocation.
7. Record a Payment Voucher (F5) for the telephone expense.
8. Select the Telephone Expense Allocation class.
9. TallyPrime automatically allocates the expense according to the defi ned
percentages.
10. Save the voucher and verify the Cost Centre Report.
